   "text": "The villagers of the Southern Shore celebrate the work that helped their settlement survive. Competitors display their creations near the village center while elders tell the children how much knowledge was once lost.\n(Cook1) prepares a familiar fish-and-root stew; (cook2) offers an unusual fruit, herb and roasted shellfish dish. A visiting elder who once fed the entire village during a lean season takes the judging spoon.\n\"If this is meant to honor our survival,\" (judge.he/she) says, \"it must first be survivable.\" The crowd laughs uneasily.",
